{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788297091896,"sessionID":"ses_fa130e14bffeHOCZtybDeHH22K","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_0339b71029e444c2b4d5017e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn -i \"input\\|stdin\\|source\" src/tir.rs src/input.rs src/parse.rs | head -40"},"output":"src/tir.rs:24:/// A binding the source cannot name, introduced for `|` and for `select`'s parameter.\nsrc/tir.rs:47:    /// to the unwrapped payload only when `source` is present; an absent `source` passes\nsrc/tir.rs:54:        source: Box<Tir>,\nsrc/tir.rs:58:    /// A name written in the source: today only a function parameter.\nsrc/tir.rs:61:    /// The value read from stdin.\nsrc/tir.rs:62:    Input,\nsrc/tir.rs:63:    /// Every remaining JSON value on stdin, one per line, eagerly collected into a `Vec<T>`.\nsrc/tir.rs:64:    Inputs,\nsrc/tir.rs:65:    /// The stream of lines read from stdin, read incrementally by whatever consumes it.\nsrc/tir.rs:67:    /// Stdin read as raw lines, each split on the delimiter, born `Vec<Vec<Str>>`: the\nsrc/tir.rs:68:    /// parameterized DSV source. `csv`/`tsv` arrive here with the delimiter already fixed.\nsrc/tir.rs:110:    /// separate because the result's element type is the body's rather than the source's.\nsrc/tir.rs:112:        source: Box<Tir>,\nsrc/tir.rs:117:        source: Box<Tir>,\nsrc/tir.rs:268:    /// The type stdin must have, if the program reads it.\nsrc/tir.rs:269:    pub input: Option<Type>,\nsrc/tir.rs:270:    /// The element type each line of stdin parses as, if the program reads `inputs`.\nsrc/tir.rs:271:    pub inputs: Option<Type>,\nsrc/tir.rs:272:    /// Whether the program reads `lines`. A separate flag from `input`, since the two are\nsrc/tir.rs:273:    /// unrelated readers of the same real stdin and a program using `lines` alone still needs\nsrc/tir.rs:274:    /// it connected, even though `input` is `None`.\nsrc/tir.rs:277:    /// reads the same real stdin as the other three, so it is exclusive with them.\nsrc/tir.rs:308:/// One `map`/`select` applied between reading a record and printing it, in source order (the\nsrc/tir.rs:309:/// stage nearest the source first).\nsrc/tir.rs:318:pub enum Source<'a> {\nsrc/tir.rs:319:    Inputs,\nsrc/tir.rs:330:    pub source: Source<'a>,\nsrc/tir.rs:334:/// What a stream chain bottoms out at: a source, a function's own parameter, or the local a\nsrc/tir.rs:337:    Inputs,\nsrc/tir.rs:348:/// (sources, bindings, mappers, calls -- a conditional or match yielding one is refused, and\nsrc/tir.rs:351:/// to fuse would silently materialize stdin, which is the defect the feature exists to remove.\nsrc/tir.rs:354:        Kind::Inputs => Base::Inputs,\nsrc/tir.rs:372:            source,\nsrc/tir.rs:376:            let base = flatten(source, program, stages);\nsrc/tir.rs:384:            source,\nsrc/tir.rs:388:            let base = flatten(source, program, stages);\nsrc/tir.rs:423:/// The type question `streams_inputs` used to answer by pattern match: a `jsonlines` program\nsrc/tir.rs:438:    let source = match flatten(arg, program, &mut stages) {\nsrc/tir.rs:439:        Base::Inputs => Source::Inputs,\nsrc/tir.rs:440:        Base::Lines => Source::Lines,\n","metadata":{"output":"src/tir.rs:24:/// A binding the source cannot name, introduced for `|` and for `select`'s parameter.\nsrc/tir.rs:47:    /// to the unwrapped payload only when `source` is present; an absent `source` passes\nsrc/tir.rs:54:        source: Box<Tir>,\nsrc/tir.rs:58:    /// A name written in the source: today only a function parameter.\nsrc/tir.rs:61:    /// The value read from stdin.\nsrc/tir.rs:62:    Input,\nsrc/tir.rs:63:    /// Every remaining JSON value on stdin, one per line, eagerly collected into a `Vec<T>`.\nsrc/tir.rs:64:    Inputs,\nsrc/tir.rs:65:    /// The stream of lines read from stdin, read incrementally by whatever consumes it.\nsrc/tir.rs:67:    /// Stdin read as raw lines, each split on the delimiter, born `Vec<Vec<Str>>`: the\nsrc/tir.rs:68:    /// parameterized DSV source. `csv`/`tsv` arrive here with the delimiter already fixed.\nsrc/tir.rs:110:    /// separate because the result's element type is the body's rather than the source's.\nsrc/tir.rs:112:        source: Box<Tir>,\nsrc/tir.rs:117:        source: Box<Tir>,\nsrc/tir.rs:268:    /// The type stdin must have, if the program reads it.\nsrc/tir.rs:269:    pub input: Option<Type>,\nsrc/tir.rs:270:    /// The element type each line of stdin parses as, if the program reads `inputs`.\nsrc/tir.rs:271:    pub inputs: Option<Type>,\nsrc/tir.rs:272:    /// Whether the program reads `lines`. A separate flag from `input`, since the two are\nsrc/tir.rs:273:    /// unrelated readers of the same real stdin and a program using `lines` alone still needs\nsrc/tir.rs:274:    /// it connected, even though `input` is `None`.\nsrc/tir.rs:277:    /// reads the same real stdin as the other three, so it is exclusive with them.\nsrc/tir.rs:308:/// One `map`/`select` applied between reading a record and printing it, in source order (the\nsrc/tir.rs:309:/// stage nearest the source first).\nsrc/tir.rs:318:pub enum Source<'a> {\nsrc/tir.rs:319:    Inputs,\nsrc/tir.rs:330:    pub source: Source<'a>,\nsrc/tir.rs:334:/// What a stream chain bottoms out at: a source, a function's own parameter, or the local a\nsrc/tir.rs:337:    Inputs,\nsrc/tir.rs:348:/// (sources, bindings, mappers, calls -- a conditional or match yielding one is refused, and\nsrc/tir.rs:351:/// to fuse would silently materialize stdin, which is the defect the feature exists to remove.\nsrc/tir.rs:354:        Kind::Inputs => Base::Inputs,\nsrc/tir.rs:372:            source,\nsrc/tir.rs:376:            let base = flatten(source, program, stages);\nsrc/tir.rs:384:            source,\nsrc/tir.rs:388:            let base = flatten(source, program, stages);\nsrc/tir.rs:423:/// The type question `streams_inputs` used to answer by pattern match: a `jsonlines` program\nsrc/tir.rs:438:    let source = match flatten(arg, program, &mut stages) {\nsrc/tir.rs:439:        Base::Inputs => Source::Inputs,\nsrc/tir.rs:440:        Base::Lines => Source::Lines,\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -rn -i \"input\\|stdin\\|source\" src/tir.rs src/input.rs src/parse.rs | head -40","time":{"start":1788297091894,"end":1788297091895}},"id":"prt_05ed01b2d001II0G1mEakWPyCC","sessionID":"ses_fa130e14bffeHOCZtybDeHH22K","messageID":"msg_05ed0138e0011aRWL47PDk96kM"}}
