{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788297094434,"sessionID":"ses_fa130e14bffeHOCZtybDeHH22K","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_8b1a4697c170454aa04b00f6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-http-query-sugar-research/tests/corpus/dsv_rows.yaml"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-http-query-sugar-research/tests/corpus/dsv_rows.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # The parameterized DSV source with a general delimiter: each raw line is split on the\n2: # delimiter into one row. A line with no delimiter is one whole field, the shape\n3: # `str.split(delim)` gives on every backend.\n4: program: |\n5:   dsv(\";\")\n6: \n7: input: |\n8:   a;b;c\n9:   d;e\n10:   f\n11: \n12: output: |\n13:   [[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"],[\"d\",\"e\"],[\"f\"]]\n14: \n15: node_types: [dsv]\n\n(End of file - total 15 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# The parameterized DSV source with a general delimiter: each raw line is split on the\n# delimiter into one row. A line with no delimiter is one whole field, the shape\n# `str.split(delim)` gives on every backend.\nprogram: |\n  dsv(\";\")\n\ninput: |\n  a;b;c\n  d;e\n  f\n\noutput: |\n  [[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"],[\"d\",\"e\"],[\"f\"]]\n\nnode_types: [dsv]","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-http-query-sugar-research/tests/corpus/dsv_rows.yaml","text":"# The parameterized DSV source with a general delimiter: each raw line is split on the\n# delimiter into one row. A line with no delimiter is one whole field, the shape\n# `str.split(delim)` gives on every backend.\nprogram: |\n  dsv(\";\")\n\ninput: |\n  a;b;c\n  d;e\n  f\n\noutput: |\n  [[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"],[\"d\",\"e\"],[\"f\"]]\n\nnode_types: [dsv]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":15,"totalLines":15,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/corpus/dsv_rows.yaml","time":{"start":1788297094363,"end":1788297094430}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The language has sources: `input` (single JSON value from stdin), `inputs` (every JSON value on stdin, one per line), `lines` (stream of lines). That's the \"source\" vocabulary. There's no sink vocabulary yet besides stdout printing.\n\nLet me look at how a real toylang program uses `input`, `lines`, etc. Let me check a couple corpus files and the docs. Let me look at the corpus case with inputs to understand the source syntax.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ed024cf001rlznWK5fY9wyJw","sessionID":"ses_fa130e14bffeHOCZtybDeHH22K","messageID":"msg_05ed01b490016CW3uqgwHdVMiH"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788297094434,"sessionID":"ses_fa130e14bffeHOCZtybDeHH22K","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_8d378d77728e43cbab17a7cf","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-http-query-sugar-research/tests/corpus/adults.yaml"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-http-query-sugar-research/tests/corpus/adults.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # The emitted code is pinned for the three backends whose handling of this program says\n2: # something the output cannot: JavaScript hoists, Go declares a struct per record type,\n3: # and Python needs no declarations at all.\n4: program: |\n5:   fn adults(db: {users: Vec<{name: Str, age: Int}>}) -> Vec<Str> =\n6:       db.users | select(.age >= 18) | .[].name\n7: \n8:   adults input\n9: \n10: input: |\n11:   {\"users\": [{\"name\": \"ada\", \"age\": 36}, {\"name\": \"bo\", \"age\": 9}]}\n12: \n13: output: |\n14:   [\"ada\"]\n15: \n16: snapshot: [js, go, py]\n17: \n18: node_types: [application, compare.ge, input, int, local, pipe, projection, selection.narrow, var]\n\n(End of file - total 18 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# The emitted code is pinned for the three backends whose handling of this program says\n# something the output cannot: JavaScript hoists, Go declares a struct per record type,\n# and Python needs no declarations at all.\nprogram: |\n  fn adults(db: {users: Vec<{name: Str, age: Int}>}) -> Vec<Str> =\n      db.users | select(.age >= 18) | .[].name\n\n  adults input\n\ninput: |\n  {\"users\": [{\"name\": \"ada\", \"age\": 36}, {\"name\": \"bo\", \"age\": 9}]}\n\noutput: |\n  [\"ada\"]\n\nsnapshot: [js, go, py]\n\nnode_types: [application, compare.ge, input, int, local, pipe, projection, selection.narrow, var]","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-http-query-sugar-research/tests/corpus/adults.yaml","text":"# The emitted code is pinned for the three backends whose handling of this program says\n# something the output cannot: JavaScript hoists, Go declares a struct per record type,\n# and Python needs no declarations at all.\nprogram: |\n  fn adults(db: {users: Vec<{name: Str, age: Int}>}) -> Vec<Str> =\n      db.users | select(.age >= 18) | .[].name\n\n  adults input\n\ninput: |\n  {\"users\": [{\"name\": \"ada\", \"age\": 36}, {\"name\": \"bo\", \"age\": 9}]}\n\noutput: |\n  [\"ada\"]\n\nsnapshot: [js, go, py]\n\nnode_types: [application, compare.ge, input, int, local, pipe, projection, selection.narrow, var]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":18,"totalLines":18,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/corpus/adults.yaml","time":{"start":1788297094408,"end":1788297094432}},"id":"prt_05ed024de001Ggm8m422WUtx7o","sessionID":"ses_fa130e14bffeHOCZtybDeHH22K","messageID":"msg_05ed01b490016CW3uqgwHdVMiH"}}
